# The national-prefix module (issue #706 §4): the parameterized NSB token
# layer. DIN, BS, NF, SS-, NEN-, UNE-, ÖNORM, CAN/CSA are the same module
# with a different parameter — `BS EN ISO 9001:2015`, `NF EN ISO 9001`,
# `SS-EN ISO 9001`, `NEN-EN-ISO 9001` are one definition composed with
# this module and a different `prefixes` value.
#
# The parameter is the module's whole point: the tokens are DATA, so the
# wizard (#406) offers national.prefix as a parameterized form field.

module: national.prefix
version: 1
title: "The national-standards-body prefix"
description: >-
  The national body's own head token(s), parameterized per composing
  definition. The national token leads the reference; an adoption overlay
  or an inner document may follow it.

parameters:
  prefixes:
    type: tokens
    required: true
    description: >-
      The NSB head tokens, verbatim as printed ("DIN", "BS", "NF",
      "SS-", "NEN-", "UNE-", "ÖNORM", "CAN/CSA"). Each becomes a
      head-dispatch token of the composed flavor.

identity:
  composition: wrapper-with-adopted
  base_module: iso.inner
  adopted_field: adopted

hooks:
  national_amendment: >-
    National irregularity on the amendment face — the BS "+A1" national
    amendment numbering is the canonical example. Where a body exceeds
    the parameters, it drops to a coded hook beside its definition.
  redating: >-
    National re-dating (the adopted year replaced by the national
    publication year) is a body-specific rule, not a module parameter.
